tests:
  unit:
    waived: "measurement-only WU - produces recorded numbers and a corpus, changes no code. The diff is two T3 docs (plan, result) and nothing else; git diff --name-only over base..tip touches no src/, xtask/, tests/, ui/src/ or ui/e2e/ path, so there is no function added or changed for a unit test to cover. Pre-registered in the epic plan's E2E test plan in this exact wording."
  integration:
    waived: "measurement-only WU - produces recorded numbers and a corpus, changes no code. W2 adds no mechanism with a bounded contract: the replay is a procedure an agent session executes, not code that ships. Same pre-registration."
  e2e:
    waived: "Epic-level, not WU-level. The epic's e2e is a full review run under the adopted configuration asserting verdict parity against the baseline sweep; W2 produces the baseline half of that comparison and adopts no configuration, so it cannot carry the flow."
verified:
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc green on docs/work/2026-09-07-crscope-w2-plan.html (wu-plan) and docs/work/2026-09-07-crscope-w2-result.html (wu-result)."
  - "Reproducibility check 1 of 4 (pinned scopes): all three timed entries recorded as full base and head SHAs plus the diff_sha256 their historical cr note carries - 083fda7e6fc8, 7caf7b49148f, ecd22bb53edd. A re-runner can prove they measured the same bytes. Independently re-verified byte-for-byte against the cr notes on be340845..d1ed2861, b5664d9b..d2d9a89e and b9e0bdbb..3d78f2c9 in review round 3."
  - "Reproducibility check 2 of 4 (self-reported timings): FAILED AS SPECIFIED, and this is why the plan demanded both clocks. Five of 106 roles reported an END later than the orchestrator's wall clock at the moment their result arrived - impossible, not merely doubtful; one claimed 575 s where the harness measured 223 s. Every figure in the result is the harness's own duration. The rule is recorded because a role that mis-transcribes its own clock cannot be caught from inside its own report."
  - "Reproducibility check 3 of 4 (n stated per figure): the complex band's verify and verified-recall figures rest on n=2. Visible in the outcome table in words, in the phase table as run 3's unfilled verify cells, and in the recall table as the two runs it names. The per-role table was the exception - its pooled verifier row spans all three runs, run 3's lone survivor included - and now carries a note stating that grain. No single-run number is presented as a baseline."
  - "Reproducibility check 4 of 4 (deviations declared): nine, and the enumeration matches the result's deviations table row for row - (1) the design probe never ran, (2) complex verify is n=2, (3) self-reported role clocks proved unreliable and the harness clock is authoritative, (4) three solo calibration probes excluded, (5) sections 2 and 6 omitted from every replay, (6) cr notes withheld from every role, (7) the rubric pinned to this tip's blob 755e70bc, (8) identical claims from two finders counted as one candidate, (9) three phase paths are lower bounds rather than measurements. Rows 1 and 2 are the two shortfalls below. Cold replay targets are a property of the replay environment, recorded in the result's evidence table - they are not a deviation, and an earlier version of this check wrongly counted them as one in place of row 3."
  - "A FIFTH CHECK THE PLAN DID NOT ASK FOR, and the one that would have caught the most: the derived layer recomputed mechanically from the appendix. Asserted and run - no phase critical path shorter than a role inside it, every per-role min/median/max recomputed (pooled verifier medians 89 s from 31 values simple, 90 s from 13 moderate, 111 s from 14 complex as the mean of the two middle values), every run path equal to find plus verify, every candidate count matched against both the appendix's own count and the number of verifiers that phase spawned, and the role totals summing to 45 finders and 58 verifiers. It reports exactly the three documented lower bounds of deviation 9 and nothing else. EIGHT of the defects the four review rounds found lived in this layer and are caught this way - a ratio, three medians, a superlative, three phase paths. The rest were not and need different checks, which follow-up 7 now names: two label counts recomputed against cr notes outside the document, one wrong causal claim, a dead anchor, unrendered diagram labels, and several places where prose disagreed with the table beside it. The plan's four checks were all satisfiable without ever making the arithmetic comparison at all."
  - "106 roles returned: 45 finders across 9 complete find phases (5 each), 58 verifiers across 8 complete verify phases (9/11/11 simple, 8/3/2 moderate, 8/5/1 complex), 3 calibration probes; a further 6 verifiers were killed by the rate limit. Every per-role duration is in the result's appendix, which is the primary record - the session log does not outlive the session."
  - "Verdict parity held 8 of 8 against the historical notes (all FAIL), which the result records as a weak instrument rather than a pass: it held while recall was 0/5."
waived_layers_replaced_by: "The plan required reproducibility of the measurement in place of a suite, in four numbered checks. ONE passed as written - check 1. Check 2 failed and the failure is reported as a finding about the instrument. Check 3 was overclaimed and is corrected here. Check 4's own enumeration was found miscounted in round 2 and corrected. And the check that mattered most was absent from the plan entirely - recomputing the derived layer from the raw one - so it was added, run, and recorded above. Four checks that cannot see the arithmetic they certify are not a substitute for a suite; five that can is closer."
note: "TWO SHORTFALLS AND TWO INSTRUMENT FAILURES, all stated as such. Shortfalls: a session API rate limit (HTTP 429) killed complex run 3's verify phase mid-flight - six of seven verifiers died, one returned - so the complex band carries n=2 for verify; and the design probe (42875df5..9b16798c, n=3 find-only) never ran, so the section 3b design finder has NO baseline, which is exactly what plan v2's amendment existed to deliver. The rate limit is only the second cause of that one: the probe was 18 roles against the bands' 109 and was scheduled last, so the cheapest plan-mandated deliverable was the one certain to be lost first, and the deviation now says so. Instrument failures: role self-timing is unusable (deviation 3), and three phase paths are shorter than a role inside them and so are recorded as lower bounds rather than measurements (deviation 9) - the session log was gone by the time review found it, so the true values are unrecoverable. Nothing is re-scoped away: the design probe is follow-up 1, the complex band's n=2 verify is follow-up 8, and the missing check is follow-up 7. Review round 5 found that the second shortfall had been claimed as follow-up 2 since the first result commit, which is the stage-1 recall rule and not this - declared, called handed-forward, and owed to nobody until row 8. What did complete: simple n=3 whole, moderate n=3 whole, complex r1 and r2 whole plus r3's find phase whole. The substantive results do not depend on the missing runs or on the three bounded cells - each bound moves its cell by at most 11 s, recall was 0/5 on the moderate band in all three of its complete runs, and the verdict flips are counted only over judgements that actually returned."
